<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thermon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thermon was the chief sanctuary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aetolians">Aetolians</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> Thermios, near Lake Trichonida. Its temple of Apollo, built in the late 7th century BCE, is among the earliest known Greek temples, and the site served as the meeting place and treasury of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aetolian-league">Aetolian League</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-macedon">Philip V of Macedon</a> sacked it in 218 BCE.</p></div>
